From 2bc97db78d93847ba411bae237d53e496b6ffd6d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eric Yang <eric.yang.wiwynn@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 23 Apr 2026 08:54:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] storage: Add Drive.Reset action with association-based state
 lookup

Add Redfish Drive.Reset action support for drives managed by
phosphor-drive-state-manager. The state daemon publishes its D-Bus
object on a separate path from inventory and links the two with an
association tuple. bmcweb follows the /state association from the
inventory object to discover whether a state manager exists for a given
drive.

When a state object is found, the Drive GET response gains an Actions
block and Status.State reflects the drive power state and rebuild
status. The Drive.Reset POST route maps Redfish ResetType values to
D-Bus RequestedDriveTransition. A ResetActionInfo route advertises
the supported reset types.

Tested:
On a Yosemite5 platform with entity-manager exposing Item.Drive
inventory objects (ssd0, ssd1) via JSON configuration and
phosphor-drive-state-manager providing State.Drive objects linked to
inventory via D-Bus association (simulated drives, no real NVMe power
hardware attached to targets):

  curl -sk -u root:0penBmc \
    https://<bmc>/redfish/v1/Systems/system/Storage/1/Drives/ssd0

  "Actions": {"#Drive.Reset": {
    "target": ".../Actions/Drive.Reset", ...}}
  "Status": {"State": "Enabled"}

Drive.Reset POST with each ResetType (On, ForceOff,
GracefulRestart, ForceRestart, PowerCycle) returns 200 and drives
reach expected state. After ForceOff, GET shows Status.State
StandbyOffline. After On, GET shows Enabled.

Host power-off triggers automatic drive poweroff. GET on both ssd0
and ssd1 reflects Status.State StandbyOffline. Host power-on
restores drives and GET shows Enabled.

ResetActionInfo returns all five AllowableValues. Invalid ResetType
returns 400 ActionParameterNotSupported. Non-existent drive returns
404 ResourceNotFound.

References:
[1] https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/docs/+/89404
[2] https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/phosphor-state-manager/+/89401
[3] https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/phosphor-dbus-interfaces/+/89402
[4] https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/entity-manager/+/89550

